    "result": "I rewrote `intervals.go` and added `Add`, `Remove` and `Free` plus tests for each. I could not run the tests: the environment asked for approval on `go test` and gave none. Run `go test ./...` to check them.\n\nThe old `Normalize` had four bugs, now fixed:\n- It sorted the input slice in place, so it changed the caller's data.\n- It did not merge touching intervals, such as `[1,3)` and `[3,5)`.\n- It set the merged end to the last interval's end, not the larger end, so `[1,10)` plus `[5,6)` became `[1,6)`.\n- It kept empty and inverted intervals.\n\n`Add` copies the slice before it appends, so a caller's spare capacity is never written. `Remove` ignores an empty or inverted `x`. `Free` returns nil when `from \u003e= to`.\n\n**TLDR**\nAll four functions are done with tests, but I could not run the tests: approval was not given. Run `go test ./...`.",
